name w4-04-emitter-hunt
timeout 500
time 1999-04-14T10:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W4, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - ALLIED FORCE 1999. THE CAMPAIGN'S CENTRAL QUESTION.
# A SUPPRESSION PAIR AT THE FLOOR AGAINST A DEFENCE WHOSE ONLY LIVE ANTENNA IS ITS NODE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w4-allied-force.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: none - it IS the control, of BOTH w4-05-emcon.fbm (ONE line: the node's `set emcon`) and
# w4-06-decoy.fbm (ONE fact: three more emitters).
#
# THE ANCHOR: 50 F-16CJ Block 50 with AGM-88 flew against Yugoslav radars that were "dispersed, radars
# mostly not emitting", concealed under weather and mountainous terrain, with extensive use of decoys
# [T3]/[T4]. That is not one battery's trick, it is the DOCTRINE of this air defence, and it is why
# this campaign exists. W4's spec calls this mission "unbuildable today; specified so the shape is on
# record", on gap `C1`.
#
# RULE 7 - A BLOCKED MISSION IS RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE TREE, NOT AGAINST A GAP'S STATUS LINE - AND
# EVERY BLOCKER HAS CLOSED:
#   C1  CLOSED 2026-07-28. `p18` `sa6` `sa3` are positions that find, track, gate an envelope and fire
#       a doctrinal salvo out of a finite magazine; `set emcon hold` is a PASSIVE RECEIVER and not a
#       timer, which is exactly "a radar that emits and stops"
#   C22 CLOSED 2026-07-28. A node cues a fire unit's ANTENNA and can never create a track; a member
#       declares its own `autonomy`, so a defence can be built that is blind without its node
#   C8/C27 BUILT 2026-07-28. `agm88` is a round whose seeker IS a warning receiver - a bearing, an
#       elevation and a received power, never a range - and `set attack_mode arm` is the release cue
#   C2  CLOSED. This file declares its own clock
# So the spec's "unbuildable" is superseded, and the mission is flown.
#
# THE ARENA, every coordinate [SET] inside the anchor's Kosovo engagement zone. Ingress west->east.
#   `k4nod` P-18 "Spoon Rest D"  42.78000 20.95000, `emcon free`, the net's CONTROL. Its published
#                                elevation coverage is -5 deg .. +15 deg [T4], and that number decides
#                                this sortie
#   `k4sam` 2K12 Kub             42.70000 21.10000, `emcon hold`, `autonomy hold`, 3 rounds
#   `k4sa3` S-125 Neva           42.62000 21.05000, `emcon hold`, `autonomy hold`, 4 rounds
#   `k4tgt` target_soft          42.70000 21.15000  ·  `k4hgr` target_hard 42.67000 21.18000
#   the Weasels                  spawn 42.78000 20.70560 = exactly 20.0 km west of the node, at the
#                                anchor's 15,000 ft floor
#   the strikers                 spawn 42.70000 20.55000, 49.1 km west of their aim point, at the floor
# NOTHING BLUE RADIATES. All four F-16 fly `set fcr_mode off`: a strike pair on a briefed steerpoint
# has no reason to, and a Weasel whose seeker is a receiver has less. That is what makes the defence's
# own emission the ONLY thing on the air in this file.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION: the F-16CJ Block 50 IS the aircraft of this anchor and the
# module is an F-16, so the SEAD side is the historical type. NO CATALOGUE ROW FLIES IN ANY W4 FILE -
# see the campaign file for the four rows W4 wanted and why each is refused; the MiG-29s of sorties
# 07/08/10 are the 127th's own aircraft and need no substitution at all.
#
# THE TWO ENGAGEMENTS ARE SEPARATED IN SPACE AND THE FILE HAS ONLY ONE FIGHT: `FBMissionRunner` ends
# the whole run at the first flight-monitor K.O., so no fighter flies in 04, 05 or 06.
#
# THE FOUR STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURES: see w4-01-floor.fbm. Disclosure 1 is load-bearing here - a
# dispersed defence's whole point is that terrain hides it, and this arena's terrain hides nothing, so
# every position below is found at its catalogue range gate and not at a real one.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: CAN A WEAPON THAT HEARS ONLY WHAT RADIATES KILL A DEFENCE WHOSE ONLY LIVE
# ANTENNA IS ITS EARLY-WARNING NODE?
#
# READING RULE (binding): exit 3 = TIMEOUT is expected - one `kill unit` is on a `target_hard` that
# survives its miss distance. Read, in order: (1) `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE ... mode=arm` - a BEARING and
# a CONE, with no range anywhere on the line, (2) `missile SEEKER_ACTIVE` and every `EMITTER_LOST`
# with its `tofS`, (3) where the rounds came down (`stores IMPACT crossLat/crossLon`), (4)
# `UNIT_RESULT` for `k4nod`, `k4sam`, `k4sa3`, (5) how many strikers reached release.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 77782e76709d55f7, exit 3): YES - BUT ONLY FROM UNDER THE CAMPAIGN'S OWN FLOOR.
#   the shot          `pilot ATTACK_RELEASE unit=k4wsa mode=arm class=any kind=surface-search
#                     brgDeg=-0.000255 signal=0.9984 fovDeg=40` at t=0.1 from 20.0 km - a BEARING and a
#                     CONE, and no range anywhere on the line, because this seeker has none
#   the node dies     both AGM-88 arrive: **3.82 m** (t=66.5, `damage KILL unit=k4nod`) and **1.96 m**
#                     (t=67.5). `mission SUPPRESSED ... emittingS=66.5 allowanceS=120` MET, and met
#                     because the position DIED
#   THE PRICE, AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S SHARPEST NUMBER. The Weasels fly at 3,000 m, 1,572 m UNDER the
#   anchor's own 15,000 ft floor, and they have to. ATTRIBUTION A2, a lone `p18` and one AGM-88 at
#   20.0 km with launch altitude the ONLY variable; "miss" is the distance from the impact point to the
#   position:
#     1,500 m  1,252 m short   the round never loses the emitter - it runs out of energy
#     3,000 m  **4.47 m**      KILL
#     3,500 m  **0.018 m**     KILL, last fresh look at 11.71 deg
#     4,000 m  **0.009 m**     KILL, loses the emitter at tofS 27.8 s and gets it back on the way down
#     4,100 m  **0.049 m**     KILL, last fresh look 13.90 deg
#     4,150 m  **0.104 m**     KILL, last fresh look 14.24 deg
#     4,200 m  **74.8 m**      MISS, last fresh look at **15.00 deg**
#     4,400 m  **1,219 m**     MISS, last fresh look at **15.00 deg**
#     4,572 m  **2,484 m**     MISS, last fresh look at **15.00 deg**   <- the anchor's floor
#   The mechanism is measured to two decimals and it is not a tuning constant: the last FRESH look of
#   every failing shot is at an elevation, computed AT THE POSITION, of exactly 15.00 deg - the
#   catalogue's `SearchElCenterDeg 5 + SearchElHalfDeg 10` [T4]. The round climbs out of the top of the
#   radar's own coverage, coasts on a rate that is four seconds old and is never brought back.
#   SO THE ANTI-RADIATION SHOT AGAINST A METRIC EARLY-WARNING SET HAS A WINDOW WITH A CEILING, AND
#   NATO'S OWN ALTITUDE FLOOR SITS 372-422 m ABOVE IT: 15,000 ft = 4,572 m, and the boundary on this
#   geometry is between 4,150 and 4,200 m = 13,620-13,780 ft. A crew that obeys the floor cannot hold
#   this radar; a crew that breaks it is in the layer the floor exists for (sortie 03).
#   THE FIRE UNITS ARE NEVER TOUCHED AND THEY SHOOT ANYWAY: the node cues both at t=8.0 (`net CUE` - a
#   bearing, a range and an altitude the crew types into its own antenna), and the S-125 fires **all
#   four V-601 at the WEASELS** (t=40.8/43.3/74.2/76.8, brg 279-289 deg). The 2K12 fires nothing: it is
#   still inside its 26 s reaction when the node dies and the cue expires. Zero arrivals either way.
#   THE STRIKE GOES THROUGH: 2 of 2 strikers release; `k4tgt` DESTROYED at `aimErrM` 48.07 m, `k4hgr`
#   (`target_hard`, needs ~8 m for an Mk-82) INTACT at 54.15 m.

net kosnet
  control k4nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member k4nod
  member k4sam autonomy hold
  member k4sa3 autonomy hold

unit k4wsa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws4 1
  spawn 42.78000 20.70560 3000 90.0 480     # 20.0 km west of the node, AT the floor
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class any
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.78000 20.90000 3000 480
  wp 42.78000 20.50000 3000 480
  objective suppress unit k4nod emitting 120
  objective survive

unit k4wsb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws4 2
  spawn 42.75000 20.70560 3150 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class any
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.75000 20.90000 3150 480
  wp 42.75000 20.50000 3150 480
  objective survive

unit k4stra
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st4 1
  spawn 42.70000 20.55000 4572 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.70000 21.15000 4572 450
  wp 42.70000 20.60000 4572 450
  objective kill unit k4tgt
  objective survive

unit k4strb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st4 2
  spawn 42.67000 20.55000 4720 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 42.67000 21.18000 4720 450
  wp 42.67000 20.60000 4720 450
  objective kill unit k4hgr
  objective survive

unit k4nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 42.78000 20.95000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon free

unit k4sam
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.10000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 3

unit k4sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 42.62000 21.05000 ground 270.0 0
  set emcon hold
  set rounds 4

unit k4tgt
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 42.70000 21.15000 ground 90.0 0

unit k4hgr
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 42.67000 21.18000 ground 90.0 0
